OL,3,GNEWSAMixed feelings as beach cafe
OL,4,Agranted temporary lease
OL,5,
OL,6,FA beach-front cafe has been given a
OL,7,Ffurther 11 months to operate, but
OL,8,Fsupporters have been left with "mixed
OL,9,Ffeelings" by the decision.
OL,11,FSOBO Beach has been told it can remain
OL,12,Fon the site in Southbourne, Dorset,
OL,13,Funtil Bournemouth Christchurch and
OL,14,FPoole (BCP) Council's "preferred
OL,15,Fbidder" is ready to take over the 20
OL,16,Fyear lease.
OL,18,FCampaigners have gathered more than
OL,19,F10,000 signatures in support of the
OL,20,Fcafe being allowed to stay at the site
OL,21,Fpermanently.
OL,23,APub: 14-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB S Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
